2. Publication of Changes (Affero / AGPL Copyleft)

Modifications are allowed, but they are not private forever once you
distribute the Software or let others use a modified version over a network.
You must publish your changes under this License as set out below.

2.1 Distribution of binaries or source

If you Convey the Software (modified or not) in object or executable form,
you must also provide the Corresponding Source of that version to recipients
under this License, using one of the AGPLv3-compliant methods (accompany the
binaries, a written offer, network server access, or peer-to-peer as in
AGPLv3). The Corresponding Source must include all of your modifications.

2.2 Network use of a modified version (Affero obligation)

If you modify the Software and run a modified version that users can interact
with remotely through a computer network, you must offer those users a
prominent opportunity to receive the Corresponding Source of that modified
version from a network server at no charge, under this License, as required
by AGPLv3 section 13. This applies even if you do not distribute binaries and
even if you do not charge for access.

2.3 Same license; no closed modifications

Any modified version or derivative work that you Convey, or whose
Corresponding Source you must offer under Section 2.1 or 2.2, must be
licensed as a whole under this License (vzctl Public License v1), including
Sections 3–6. You may not keep required Corresponding Source proprietary,
nor relicense required Corresponding Source under plain AGPL or any other
terms that omit Sections 3–6.

2.4 What must be published

"Your changes" means all modifications, additions, and derivative material
that are part of the Corresponding Source for the version you Convey or
expose to network users — including patches, new modules that form part of
the covered work, and build/install scripts needed to reproduce that version.

2.5 Private internal use

If you modify the Software solely for private use inside your organization
and you neither Convey it to third parties nor provide Network interaction
with that modified version to third parties, Section 2 does not by itself
require you to publish those internal-only changes. As soon as you Convey or
provide such Network interaction, Sections 2.1–2.4 apply.


3. No Sale

You may not Sell the Software.

Prohibited (non-exhaustive):
  - selling vzctl, forks, or derivatives as a product;
  - paid redistribution of source or binaries;
  - paid "enterprise", "pro", "supported build", or branded forks whose
    primary deliverable is the Software;
  - charging for download, installers, container images, or access to the
    Software itself.

Allowed:
  - using the Software free of charge inside your own organization, including
    for commercial internal operations;
  - charging for genuine professional services that are not a pretext for
    Selling the Software (for example consulting, custom integration,
    training, or time-and-materials support), provided the Software itself
    remains available under this License at no charge and is not the product
    being sold.

Section 3 does not waive Section 2: if you Convey or provide Network
interaction with a modified version in connection with otherwise allowed
activity, you must still publish Corresponding Source as required above.


4. No Commercial Bundling / No Open-Source Polishing

You may not Bundle the Software into a Commercial Product.

This section prohibits commercial redistributors and "open-source polishers"
that package, wrap, rebrand, or integrate the Software into a paid or
proprietary offering.

Prohibited (non-exhaustive):
  - embedding or shipping the Software inside a paid hypervisor, DevOps,
    virtualization, or lab-management product;
  - proprietary commercial GUIs, control planes, or appliances that
    redistribute or require the Software as a bundled component;
  - OEM / white-label distributions of the Software;
  - combining the Software with proprietary code into one Commercial Product
    that customers receive or run.

Allowed:
  - running the Software as a standalone tool in a commercial environment;
  - using the Software to build, host, or operate your own workloads and
    internal infrastructure;
  - combining the Software only with software that is itself licensed under
    this License or under AGPLv3 (or another strong copyleft that keeps the
    combination non-proprietary), provided the result is not Sold and is not
    offered as a Commercial Product, and provided Section 2 is satisfied.


5. No Commercial Hosted Offering of the Software

You may not Provide as a Service a Commercial Product whose primary purpose
or primary value is access to the Software or a thin wrapper around it.

Prohibited (non-exhaustive):
  - "managed vzctl", "vzctl cloud", or equivalent paid hosted offerings;
  - multi-tenant SaaS control planes that expose the Software's core
    functionality to paying customers;
  - paid remote access to forks/derivatives that are substantially the
    Software.

Allowed:
  - using the Software privately to operate your own unrelated services
    (the Software is infrastructure you run, not the product you sell to
    customers);
  - employees/contractors of your organization using the Software on your
    behalf, without providing the Software's functionality as a paid product
    to third parties.

If a permitted use still involves Network interaction with a modified
version by third parties, Section 2.2 applies.


6. No Circumvention

You may not do indirectly what this License prohibits directly, including
through affiliates, resellers, agents, "partner" SKUs, separate download
portals, dual packaging, or contracts that effectively Sell, Bundle, or
Provide as a Service the Software in violation of Sections 3–5, or that
avoid the source-publication duties in Section 2.

Any attempt to relicense, sublicense, or redistribute the Software under
plain AGPL or any other terms that omit Sections 2–6 is void and is a
breach of this License.


